@startuml
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
autonumber
title Diagrama Devoluciones 3: GET /api/v1/refunds/:id (Detalle y pantalla de decisión)

actor "Aprobador / Vendedor" as User
participant "App Web" as Web
participant "Gateway Controller" as Gateway
participant "Refund Order Service" as Service
participant "refund_orders DB" as OrdersDB
participant "refund_order_details DB" as DetailsDB
participant "refund_order_detail_sources DB" as SourcesDB
participant "refund_order_detail_photos DB" as PhotosDB
participant "refund_reasons DB" as ReasonsDB
participant "refund_workflow_instances DB" as InstanceDB
participant "refund_workflow_instance_levels DB" as LevelsDB
participant "refund_workflow_actions DB" as ActionsDB
participant "refund_order_detail_decisions DB" as DecisionsDB
participant "Clientes / SAP\n(servicio externo)" as Sales
participant "Role Directory Client\n(servicio externo)" as RoleDir

User -> Web: Abre una nota de la bandeja
Web -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/refunds/1001
Gateway -> Service: getRefundOrderDetail(refundOrderId: 1001, actor)

Service -> OrdersDB: 1. findRefundOrder(1001)
OrdersDB --> Service: order (note_number, split_sequence, document_type,\nstatus, source_refund_order_id, total, justification, replacement_date)

Service -> Service: 2. assertVisibility(order, actor)
note right of Service
  Un rol "solo mis documentos" que pide la
  nota de otro vendedor recibe 404, no 403:
  no se revela la existencia del documento.
end note

Service -> DetailsDB: 3. findDetails(1001)
note right of DetailsDB
  Todas las líneas, ACTIVE y DISSOCIATED.
  Las DISSOCIATED se muestran tachadas con
  el enlace a la nota que se las llevó.
end note
DetailsDB --> Service: details[] (product_id, source_quantity, quantity,\nprice_unit, line_status, reason, notes)

Service -> SourcesDB: 3.1a findSourcesByDetails(detailIds)
note right of SourcesDB
  Los orígenes de cada línea: factura,
  documento SAP, lote, vencimiento y cuánto
  sale de cada uno.
end note
SourcesDB --> Service: sources[]

Service -> PhotosDB: 3.1b findPhotosByDetails(detailIds)
note right of PhotosDB
  ORDER BY sort_order. Es lo primero que abre
  el revisor: si storage_key se firma en cada
  lectura, la URL se genera acá.
end note
PhotosDB --> Service: photos[]

Service -> ReasonsDB: 3.1c findReasons(details.reason)
note right of ReasonsDB
  Da la etiqueta visible del motivo y qué
  campos exige, para que el detalle muestre
  lote y vencimiento solo cuando aplican.
end note
ReasonsDB --> Service: reasons[]

Service -> InstanceDB: 4. findInstances(1001)
note right of InstanceDB
  Todos los intentos, no solo el vigente:
  el intento anterior queda como evidencia.
end note
InstanceDB --> Service: instances[] (attempt, status, current_level_order,\nreactivated_from_instance_id)

Service -> LevelsDB: 5. findInstanceLevels(instanceIds)
LevelsDB --> Service: levels[] (level_order, level_name, role_code,\nmin_amount, max_amount, decision_mode, status,\nfirst_viewed_at, started_at, finished_at)

Service -> ActionsDB: 6. findActionsTimeline(instanceIds)
ActionsDB --> Service: actions[] (action, actor, comment, reason,\nsystem_summary, amount_before, amount_after, created_at)

Service -> DecisionsDB: 7. findLevel1Decisions(itemSelectionActionIds)
DecisionsDB --> Service: decisions[] (refund_order_detail_id, decision)

Service -> OrdersDB: 8. findSplitFamily(noteNumber, 1001)
note right of OrdersDB
  Nota origen (source_refund_order_id) y
  disociadas hijas: comparten note_number
  y se ordenan por split_sequence.
end note
OrdersDB --> Service: relatedOrders[]

Service -> Sales: 9. getClientAndInvoiceData(order.owner_id, details.productIds)
note right of Sales
  NIT, canal, sector y el documento SAP de la
  factura de origen no viven en nuestras
  tablas: se piden a Ventas/SAP.
end note
Sales --> Service: clientDetails + invoiceRefs[]

Service -> RoleDir: 10. resolveApproversByRole(openLevel.roleCode)
RoleDir --> Service: employees[]

Service -> Service: 11. buildDecisionContext(order, levels, actions, employees, actor)
note right of Service
  Deriva para el FE:
  - canDecide: hay nivel abierto, el actor
    pertenece al rol y no firmó todavía
  - showItemCheckboxes: solo si el nivel
    abierto tiene decision_mode =
    'ITEM_SELECTION'
  - firmas recibidas / necesarias
  - plazo restante del nivel (SLA)
  - posición "Nivel 2 de 4"
end note

Service --> Gateway: refundOrderDetailResponse
Gateway --> Web: 200 OK
Web --> User: Renderiza cabecera, líneas con fotos, familia de la nota y el historial
@enduml
